# .gitleaks-allowlist — human-curated false-positive list for labalyst/labalyst-runbooks
#
# Every entry MUST include:
#   1. The exact string or regex being allowlisted
#   2. The rule ID it would otherwise match
#   3. A one-line justification
#   4. The PR number where it was added (review by platform lead required)
#
# Format: see https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks#configuration — this file
# is referenced from .gitleaks.toml [allowlist] paths so its own contents
# never trigger scans.
#
# Example entry (uncomment and adapt; do not commit example UUIDs as live):
#
#   # rule: tenant-uuid
#   # justification: example UUID used in `db-connection-pool-exhaustion.md`
#   #                §3 "How to find the offending tenant" — synthetic, never
#   #                allocated to a real tenant per PRD §9.
#   # PR: #N
#   00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#
# The allowlist starts empty. Additions require platform-lead review on the
# same PR — no self-approval (README "Contributing" section).
